  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0217 database is designed to manage a library system, allowing administrators to manage users, schools, books, and their various relationships. The admin table stores information about the system administrators, with each admin having a unique username and password. The school table contains details about each school, including its name, email, principal's name, address, and phone number. The user table represents individual users, who can be students, teachers, or handlers, and each user has a unique username, password, and school affiliation. The book table stores information about each book, including its ISBN, title, summary, publisher, page count, language, and image. The category table contains a list of categories, and the book_category table links books to their respective categories. The author table stores information about authors, and the book_author table links books to their authors. The key_words table stores keywords associated with each book, and the stores table tracks the availability of books in each school. The applications table manages borrowing requests, tracking the status of each application, and the review table stores user reviews of books, including their evaluation, rating, and approval status. The database enforces various constraints to ensure data integrity, such as unique usernames and email addresses for admins and users, and constraints on the number of available copies of a book in a school.",
  "gold_question": "School Library Management System \n\n1) Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a School Library Management System for public schools to streamline library operations. The system will facilitate the management of library resources, ensuring that technological needs for efficient library management are met.\n\n2) Objectives\n\n- Establish a centralized system for managing school libraries.\n- Enable efficient registration and administration of books and user information.\n- Facilitate borrowing, returning, and reserving books.\n- Allow user review and rating of books.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Network School Library Administrator: Manages schools, appoints library operators, and handles database management.\n- School Library Operator: Manages book data, user approvals, and supervises borrowing activities.\n- Students and Teachers: Register, view, and borrow books, make reservations, and submit reviews.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- School Management: Register each school with details including name, contact information, and key personnel.\n- Book Management: Maintain comprehensive details about each book—title, publisher, authors, category, etc.\n- User Roles & Authentication:\n  - Admins register and approve library operators.\n  - Operators manage library operations and user interactions.\n  - Students and teachers register, view, borrow, and review books.\n- Borrowing & Reservations:\n  - Students: Borrow up to 2 books/week.\n  - Teachers: Borrow up to 1 book/week.\n  - Reservations are limited by borrowing capacity and expire after 1 week if not fulfilled.\n- Reviews & Ratings: Users can submit reviews and ratings which need approval from library operators.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Ensure secure user authentication and authorization processes.\n- Support robust data management, including backups and restorations.\n- Facilitate user-friendly interface for all functionalities.\n- Scale to manage multiple public school libraries efficiently.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0217.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0217\nCREATE TABLE `admin` (\n  `admin_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`admin_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `school` (\n  `school_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  `principal_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`school_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `school_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`school_id`) REFERENCES `school` (`school_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `isbn` varchar(13) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `summary` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `publisher` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `page_count` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `language` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `image` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `category` (\n  `category_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`category_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book_category` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `category_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`, `category_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_category_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `book_category_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`category_id`) REFERENCES `category` (`category_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `author` (\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`author_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book_author` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`, `author_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_author_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `book_author_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`author_id`) REFERENCES `author` (`author_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `key_words` (\n  `keyword_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `word` varchar(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`keyword_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book_key_words` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `keyword_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`, `keyword_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_key_words_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `book_key_words_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`keyword_id`) REFERENCES `key_words` (`keyword_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `stores` (\n  `store_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `school_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `available_copies` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`store_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `stores_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`school_id`) REFERENCES `school` (`school_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `stores_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `applications` (\n  `application_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`application_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `applications_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `applications_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `review` (\n  `review_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `evaluation` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `rating` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `approval_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`review_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `review_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `review_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
